+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+The client requests a page of its own conversation summaries with `{"type":"list_conversations","limit":2,"before":{"updatedAt":"2026-01-15T14:30:00.000Z","sessionId":"abc"}}`. `limit` is optional and, when present, is an integer from 1 through 200; `before` is optional and, when present, has both an ISO datetime `updatedAt` and a string `sessionId`. Malformed fields receive `INVALID_MESSAGE`, whether history is enabled or not ([validated by: accepts a list request and rejects malformed limits and composite cursors](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L92)).
+
+| Field              | Type    | Required | Description                                   |
+| ------------------ | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`             | string  | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                        |
+| `limit`            | integer | No       | Number of rows, from 1 through 200            |
+| `before.updatedAt` | string  | No       | ISO datetime of the preceding page's last row |
+| `before.sessionId` | string  | No       | Session id of that same row                   |
+
+The frame carries no authoritative user id. The server reads the authenticated user from the connection, ignores any extra `userId` in the frame, passes `limit` and `before` to `listFor`, and answers one `conversation_list` containing that user's summaries, newest first. Each row has only `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `entryCount`; the times are ISO strings on the wire. A client can reconnect with a row's `?sessionId=` to resume it when `transport.resume` is enabled ([validated by: lists only the connected owner’s rows in newest-first order, pages with the wire cursor, and resumes a selected row](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L117)).
+
+`transport.history.enabled` is a separate opt-in and defaults to off. A disabled history feature or a store without `listFor` receives `UNSUPPORTED`, while a store failure receives `SERVER_ERROR` without store details; neither failure is represented as an empty list, and the socket remains open ([validated by: answers disabled or unavailable history with UNSUPPORTED and a store failure with a safe SERVER_ERROR](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L169)).
+
+A list request is answered outside the per-session turn lock, so a conversation list can arrive before a concurrent answer's `stream_end` and never starts a turn of its own ([validated by: answers a history request while a turn is streaming, before its stream_end](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L205)).
 
